-41b6-9350-e5b09d29811b", "phase": "TEACHER", "description": "Model Scribbling, strokes and curves slowly, think aloud, and che ... (504 characters truncated) ... ibbling, strokes and curves, encourage them by name and praise their attempts.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', 'Watch each child during the activity and ask simple oral questions — point to, name or show Scribbling, strokes and curves. Tick who can do it and wh ... (44 characters truncated) ...  Assessment mode: Oral questions and observation of participation. Evidence: each child shows or names one example of Scribbling, strokes and curves.', 'Bring the children back to the circle, sing or clap about Scribbling, strokes and curves, let a few children show what they made or did, and praise each child.', '[]', '[]', '[]', '', 'Support: Sit beside the child, guide the hand or the answer for Scribbling, strokes and curves, and use bigger, simpler objects until the child succe ... (50 characters truncated) ... Scribbling, strokes and curves again with more objects or show a friend how it is done.\nGrouping: Whole-class circle time, then small guided groups.', '[]', 'generated', 0, 0, '{}', '2026-09-26 22:47:11.157928', '2026-09-26 22:47:11.157940')
