y at Colouring, encourage them by name and praise their attempts.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', 'Watch each child during the activity and ask simple oral questions — point to, name or show Colouring. Tick who can do it and who needs more help; th ... (2 characters truncated) ... e is no written test. Assessment mode: Oral questions and observation of participation. Evidence: each child shows or names one example of Colouring.', "Bring the children back to the circle, sing or clap about Colouring, let a few children show what they made or did, and praise each child. Preview the next lesson ('Colouring').", '[]', '[]', '[]', '', 'Support: Sit beside the child, guide the hand or the answer for Colouring, and use bigger, simpler objects until the child succeeds.\nExtension: Let  ... (8 characters truncated) ...  who finish early do Colouring again with more objects or show a friend how it is done.\nGrouping: Whole-class circle time, then small guided groups.', '[]', 'generated', 0, 0, '{}', '2026-09-26 22:47:40.204367', '2026-09-26 22:47:40.204417')
