nistic"}]', '[{"id": "acddeeea-b985-4644-9118-6d273bd99a7b", "phase": "TEACHER", "description": "Model Sorting objects according to colours slowly, think aloud, a ... (522 characters truncated) ... bjects according to colours, encourage them by name and praise their attempts.", "duration_minutes": 12, "resources": [], "source": "deterministic"}]', 'Watch each child during the activity and ask simple oral questions — point to, name or show Sorting objects according to colours. Tick who can do it  ... (52 characters truncated) ... ssessment mode: Classification exercise with accuracy check. Evidence: each child shows or names one example of Sorting objects according to colours.', 'Bring the children back to the circle, sing or clap about Sorting objects according to colours, let a few children show what they made or did, and praise each child.', '[]', '[]', '[]', '', 'Support: Sit beside the child, guide the hand or the answer for Sorting objects according to colours, and use bigger, simpler objects until the child ... (62 characters truncated) ... g objects according to colours again with more objects or show a friend how it is done.\nGrouping: Whole-class circle time, then small guided groups.', '[]', 'generated', 0, 0, '{}', '2026-09-26 22:48:08.809069', '2026-09-26 22:48:08.809074')
